flask was charged with primary amine (10 mmol), paraformaldehyde (4a, 20
mmol) and oxalic acid dihydrate (5a, 0.1 mol) and briefly flushed with
nitrogen. In the case of secondary amines, 10 mmol of 4a and 50 mmol of
5a were used. For amines with multiple amino functions, 10 mmol of 4a and
50 mmol of 5a were applied per methyl group to be introduced. The vessel
was closed and heated to 100°C for 1 h. and to 120°C for 10 min. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature. The white, crystalline
